<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aztec Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aztecs, Triple Alliance, Ēxcān Tlahtolōyān, Aztec</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aztec Empire was the Triple Alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texcoco">Texcoco</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlacopan">Tlacopan</a>, formed in 1428 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a> and dominated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> of Tenochtitlan. It collected tribute from a large number of subject city-states across central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>. It was conquered by Spanish forces led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a> with indigenous allies in 1519–1521, a foundational event of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aztec-empire.jpg" alt="Aztec Empire" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:Aztec Empire (orthographic projection).svg : Keepscases Derivative work : Giggette · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aztec_Empire_ME_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
